#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:157
#: fc8a637a9cf344c48a180ad704c357c8
msgid "Firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:159
#: 2e9fbe132af740bfa54bf5970e511b78
msgid "First Versions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:160
#: 066ae956c9944103abf45a7c1a60ef60
msgid "The first version of the board does not come a correct Ardupilot bootloader (it may at some future point) so it cannot be upgraded with new versions of Ardupilot firmware. ANd cecause it has not boot pin exposed, DFU loading is not possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:162
#: df0c582ba85a46eba50defa10de34080
msgid "Instead a `\"transitional\" firmware <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Tools/TransitionalFirmware/HeeWingF405/>`__  can be used and loaded like normal ArduPilot firmware (this is rev 4.3.7 Plane firmware) as a custom firmware file in Mission Planner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:164
#: 87b44c8438304a788885146e74adea30
msgid "This firmware contains the correct bootloader and it can be installed using the Mission Planner: SETUP->Install firmware \"Bootloader Update\" button after this firmware is loaded. From then on you can load any ArduPilot future firmware versions you desire, normally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-heewingf405.rst:166
#: 5a38d74917a54becb2b6ae7ac0372e1c
msgid "Firmware for this board can be found `here <https://firmware.ardupilot.org>`_ in  sub-folders labeled \"HEEWING-F405\"."
msgstr ""

